[tool_result]1	# Virtual Battery Factory 2	 3	An LLM-agent-driven, cross-scale virtual battery design platform: a fully 4	software-simulated closed loop spanning material design, cell design, and 5	safety assessment --- with no dependence on physical experiments. 6	 7	The agent executes a **protocolized governance** design loop (five-stage 8	multi-precision funnel, evaluation-and-fallback routing, mechanized 9	adjudication with an evidence-chain audit ledger) specified entirely in 10	natural language. The protocol itself is a self-contained declarative 11	artifact (`.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/`) and is 12	harness-independent by construction --- cross-harness portability runs under 13	the OpenAI Agents SDK and LangChain live in `paper/portability/`. 14	 15	## Entry point and structure 16	 17	- **`run.py`** (repo root): a thin Agent SDK launcher. It loads the protocol 18	  skill (`.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/SKILL.md`) verbatim into the 19	  agent's system prompt and drives the simulation library `python -m bda` 20	  through the harness's built-in shell tool. No custom tools are registered. 21	- The protocol skill is self-contained under 22	  `.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/`: `SKILL.md` (the protocol), 23	  `references/cli-commands.md` (command reference), 24	  `scripts/bda/` (the simulation library, pip-editable install), and 25	  `assets/` (sample cases). If the environment is missing, the agent 26	  installs it itself per protocol step 0. 27	- **Cross-harness legs** (portability experiment, §4.6 of the paper): 28	  `paper/portability/oa_sdk/run_oa.py` (OpenAI Agents SDK --- protocol 29	  injected as instructions) and `paper/portability/langchain/run_lc.py` 30	  (LangChain --- protocol loaded via an on-demand `load_skill` tool), with 31	  batch drivers `run_oa_matrix.py` / `run_lc_matrix.py`. 32	 33	## Installation 34	 35	```powershell 36	python -m venv .venv 37	.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1 38	pip install -e ".claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/scripts[dev,ml,host]" 39	``` 40	 41	External binaries (needed only for the closing true-compute endorsement; 42	each runner locates the executable via `PATH`): 43	 44	| Binary | Purpose | Source | 45	|---|---|---| 46	| xtb | Semi-empirical quantum single points (funnel pre-screen) | [github.com/grimme-lab/xtb/releases](https://github.com/grimme-lab/xtb/releases) | 47	| ORCA | True DFT endorsement (Top-3) | [faccts.de/orca](https://www.faccts.de/orca/) (academic license) | 48	| GROMACS | True MD endorsement (Top-1) | [gromacs.org/Downloads](https://www.gromacs.org/Downloads) | 49	 50	ML potentials (MACE-MP/CHGNet) ship with the `[ml]` extra. Cases with 51	`real_compute: false` need none of the above. 52	 53	### Environment bootstrap (no secrets on disk) 54	 55	Create `.env` in the repo root before running: 56	`DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=<your key>`. `run.py` resolves configuration in order 57	(existing environment variables always win): 58	 59	| Variable | Default | Meaning | 60	|---|---|---| 61	| `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` | `https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic` | Anthropic-compatible endpoint | 62	| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | `deepseek-v4-pro` | Model name | 63	| `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` | `.env`'s `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` | Credential; skipped if an Anthropic token is already set | 64	 65	Secrets are injected only into child-process environment variables, never 66	written to files, never printed. Connectivity smoke test: 67	`.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py --smoke-test`. 68	 69	## Running 70	 71	**The user's only input is natural language** --- no YAML is ever written or 72	read by hand. State the design objective directly (e.g., "design a battery 73	with energy density ≥ 400 Wh/kg and 4C fast charge without lithium 74	plating"): 75	 76	1. The skill clarifies item by item via AskUserQuestion (objective 77	   quantification / starting stage / system / ablation / true-compute 78	   switch --- all with defaults). 79	2. After clarification the skill records the criteria, writes them into the 80	   workspace audit ledger (entry 0), and executes the closed loop. 81	3. Batch experiments are launched in natural language too ("run N=3", "run 82	   the ablation matrix") --- each variant becomes a headless `run.py` session. 83	 84	The closing true-compute endorsement (`run-orca` Top-3, `run-md` Top-1) is 85	reserved for finalists. **Workspace = the run directory** (`log.jsonl`, 86	`report.html`, `csv/`, and per-stage artifact subdirectories). 87	 88	## Ablation experiments 89	 90	Ablation is declared in the task text itself (the natural-language input 91	remains the only entry point) and recorded in entry-0 metadata; the 92	governance components are fixed, always-on rules in the product protocol: 93	 94	| Declaration in the task text | What it answers | 95	|---|---| 96	| `ceiling_escalation off` | Contribution of the ceiling-assessment → material-design escalation mechanism | 97	| `exploration_force off` | Contribution of the forced 2–4 architecture variants per round | 98	| `funnel_voting off` | Contribution of three-model heterogeneous voting in the molecular funnel | 99	 100	All on = the full system (main results). See the paper 101	(`paper/main.tex`, §4.3) for the executed ablation matrix. 102	 103	## Reporting 104	 105	Closing a case auto-generates a self-contained HTML report (overview → 106	iteration trail → funnel statistics → stage results → true-compute 107	endorsement → final recommendation); open `report.html` in the workspace. 108	 109	## Tests 110	 111	```powershell 112	# fast tests (skip slow) 113	.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -m "not slow" 114	 115	# full suite (runner smoke tests auto-skip when the binary is missing) 116	.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest 117	``` 118	 119	## Repository policy 120	 121	`paper/`, `data/`, `docs/`, `references/` and `.env` are gitignored --- the 122	manuscript, experiment artifacts, and literature live locally and are not 123	versioned. The audit ledgers of finished runs (`runs/`) are likewise local. 12